  "id": "behavioral-inhibition-system",
  "term": "behavioral inhibition system",
  "definition": "The behavioral inhibition system (BIS) is an individual difference system with a strong genetic basis that is linked to negative emotion and cognition. Environmental experiences, including childhood emotional neglect, can also influence it and its effects.",
